In article <2h2uet$434@gap.cco.caltech.edu>, silly@ugcs.caltech.edu ((me)) writes:

>I'm currently a lawful caveman with lots and lots of goodies.  In addition,
>I blew a wish on the PYEC, since I figured that I ever wanted it, it'd be
>easier to get before I saw lots of artifacts.
>
>In any event, I know it's possible to change my alignment to that of an
>altar, but I was wondering what conditions had to be met.  Typically, I could
>kill my pet or a few peaceful humans and then sacrifice at an altar to 
>change alignment, but I tried the pet trick with a pet rothe and converted
>the altar instead of me.
>
>So...  What are some sure-fire ways to piss off my god enough to turn neutral
>when sacrificing at a neutral altar?  I only have one left, so I need to make
>this count.
>
>Nethack gods?

The standard sure-fire never fail-way to do this is to sacrifice a white 
unicorn (since you're lawful) corpse on the neutral altar.

Warnings:
  - Killing a unicorn lowers your luck by 5
  - Changing alignment lowers you luck by 3

Once you convert, continue to sacrifice at the altar until your new god
is happy.
